WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:01.710
Belém, Brazil.

2
00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:06.710
From 10 to 21 November
2025, it hosted COP30,

3
00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:09.050
the UN Climate Change Conference.

4
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:16.310
In 2024, China emitted 13,125
million tonnes of carbon dioxide.

5
00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:21.590
In 2000, China's share of the
world's emissions was 14.2 per cent.

6
00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:24.150
The USA's was 23.1 per cent.

7
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:29.750
By 2024, the USA's share
had fallen to 11.7 per cent,

8
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.790
while China's had
climbed to about a third.

9
00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:35.630
So are emerging powers taking charge?

10
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.110
Do they already lead?

11
00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.510
Or does the USA still decide?

12
00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:41.930
In this mission, you'll
weigh their economic,

13
00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:46.810
political and environmental power,
from the G20 to the BRICS bank.

14
00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:50.230
Then you'll test three theories
of development against their rise.

15
00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:55.720
Your mission: evaluate whether emerging
powers are really taking charge.
